WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.680
we'll, I told you yesterday that it was likely
to happen soon and it actually happened minutes

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:07.170
after we finished producing yesterday's show.

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:12.110
A Senator Kamala Harris has officially dropped
out of the presidential primary.

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:17.539
She collapsed in the polls over the last few
months, and as I told you yesterday, Kamala

00:00:17.539 --> 00:00:22.570
Harris had qualified for the next debate,
which is the sixth debate, I think on December

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:25.800
19th but the polling was just not there.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:31.000
Her fundraising was just not there, and I'll
tell you, I respect her decision to drop out

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.000
at this point in time.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.929
I'm going to address that more in a moment.

00:00:34.929 --> 00:00:36.839
Let's look at her polling first.

00:00:36.839 --> 00:00:43.800
You will see that despite hitting a national
polling high of about 15% this is her high.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:48.920
She wasn't leading, but her campaign high
was about 15% that was in the first half of

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:50.269
July.

00:00:50.269 --> 00:00:55.710
It's just been downhill for her all the way
down to a national average of barely 3% in

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:56.719
recent weeks.

00:00:56.719 --> 00:00:59.690
Now, Camila is not someone that I was supporting.

00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:04.049
She has a very troubling record in the criminal
justice system during her time as the attorney

00:01:04.049 --> 00:01:09.870
general of California, she was slippery on
healthcare to say the least.

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:14.940
She definitely, uh, brought some clever planned
attacks to the debates.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:17.690
She had one on Joe Biden in the first debate.

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:22.640
She put together an attack on Telsey Gabbert
at the last one, but it wasn't the sort of

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:29.820
substantive, vended, inspiring candidacy that
did anything for me, particularly her slipperiness

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:31.030
on healthcare.

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:37.070
She wrote in an email to her campaign supporters
to her campaign newsletter quote, my campaign

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:41.090
for president simply doesn't have the financial
resources we need to continue.

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:42.200
I'm not a billionaire.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.800
I can't fund my own campaign.

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:48.590
And as the campaign has gone on, it's become
harder and harder to raise the money we need

00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:50.230
to compete in good faith.

00:01:50.230 --> 00:01:56.200
I can't tell you my supporters and volunteers
that I have a path forward if I don't believe

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:57.200
I do.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:01.710
So to you, my supporters, it is with deep
regret, but also with deep gratitude that

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:04.960
I am suspending my campaign today.

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:09.539
Now she's absolutely correct and that's what
gets us back to the respect thing.

00:02:09.539 --> 00:02:15.159
Kamala Harris qualified for the next debate,
but she dropped out anyway because she has

00:02:15.159 --> 00:02:16.590
no chance.

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:23.719
That is what I respect because most candidates
who have no shot would keep going clogging

00:02:23.719 --> 00:02:29.151
up the debate stages because they want FaceTime,
they want the publicity, she realizes she

00:02:29.151 --> 00:02:30.151
can't win.

00:02:30.151 --> 00:02:33.099
She realizes she's not raising the money she
needs.

00:02:33.099 --> 00:02:36.709
Implicit in that also is that she doesn't
have the polling support that would allow

00:02:36.709 --> 00:02:41.470
her to raise that money and so she's dropping
out and I respect the fact that she's going

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:46.420
to clear the clear, clear the stage, and not
clog it up with folks that don't have a path

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:47.420
to victory.

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:49.930
Now there's a whole bunch of other people
who should do the same thing and we'll see

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:54.730
if anybody else does between now and December
19th immediate questions about this.

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:59.150
Number one is Kahmilah Harris angling for
a VP spot.

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:03.020
Don't know too early to talk about and quite
frankly, I'm not super interested in talking

00:03:03.020 --> 00:03:05.250
about VP stuff yet.

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:09.340
Number two, who will she support or endorse?

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:10.560
Unclear.

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:15.010
There's the idea that for demographic reasons,
maybe it would be Elizabeth Warren.

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:20.379
There's the idea that because of policy, because
she's more of a centrist, it could be Joe

00:03:20.379 --> 00:03:21.609
Biden.

00:03:21.609 --> 00:03:25.310
I don't think there's too many people thinking
that she would endorse Bernie Sanders, but

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:26.310
you never know.

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:29.290
A more immediate question is where does her
support go?

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:31.709
I actually don't think it's that important
of a question.

00:03:31.709 --> 00:03:36.879
She was pulling 3.4% on average as of yesterday
when she decided to drop out.

00:03:36.879 --> 00:03:43.019
Every candidate, if they drop out, their support
would be divided among the remaining candidates.

00:03:43.019 --> 00:03:49.279
It's not going to go all to one candidate
and however you slice and dice 3.4% it's not

00:03:49.279 --> 00:03:54.099
really going to be a game changer, so I'm
not super interested in where it is.

00:03:54.099 --> 00:03:58.249
Kamel is 3.4% go, but overall the field is
thinning.

00:03:58.249 --> 00:03:59.510
I believe at this point.

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:00.510
That's a good thing.

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:05.140
Lots of the people left don't have a shot
at the nomination.

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:09.290
They're not in the running in any of the first
four primary States, nor are they getting

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:12.739
any traction beyond two or 3% nationally.

00:04:12.739 --> 00:04:17.580
It's too late in the game to be clogging up
the debate stage when there are real differences

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:19.769
between the candidates that have a shot.

00:04:19.769 --> 00:04:24.390
I welcome a thinning of the debate stage and
we will see if it continues.

00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:29.620
Let me know not only what you think of Camila
baling, but more importantly, who else should

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:32.920
bail before the next debate?

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:34.020
I want to hear from you.

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:35.020
Leave a reply.

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:39.230
If you're watching on YouTube, we'll have
a post about this on our Instagram page at

00:04:39.230 --> 00:04:40.430
David Pakman show.

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:41.910
Follow us there

00:04:41.910 --> 00:06:10.990
and leave me your thoughts there as well.

